(a) whether Government has taken note that 531 of the 3,691 Centrally Protected Monuments are reported to be under encroachment and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has taken cognisance of CAG's observations regarding deficiencies in boundary and land ownership details of such monuments, resulting in difficulties in protecting them from encroachment and land disputes; and
(c) whether Government proposes to undertake a time-bound programme for survey, geo-referencing and digitisation of boundaries of all such monuments and integrate the same with State land records to strengthen their legal protection?

(a) whether Government maintains data on instances of biometric authentication failure faced by elderly pensioners at post offices and through IPPB doorstep banking services and if so, the details thereof during the last three years;
(b) the alternative verification mechanism, if any, available for beneficiaries whose biometric authentication does not succeed and the average time taken in such cases to complete the pension disbursal process; and
(c) the number of GDS-operated doorstep banking points currently functional in rural areas as against the sanctioned strength and whether any assessment has been made of the adequacy of doorstep banking coverage for elderly and mobility-restricted pensioners?

(a) whether the Ministry has unveiled 'PRAHAAR' as India's first comprehensive 'National Counter-Terrorism Policy and Strategy,' and if so, the date of unveiling and the key pillars thereof;
(b) the specific objectives of 'PRAHAAR' that could not be effectively addressed under the existing counter-terrorism and internal security framework;
(c) the institutional and coordination mechanisms proposed between Central and State agencies for the implementation of this policy; and
(d) the timeline for the operationalization of this strategy and the manner in which the outcomes thereof would be reviewed?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance that, as per UDISE+ 2024–25, only about 1.12 lakh schools have a dedicated special educator, leaving a large number of schools without one and if so, the reasons therefor;
(b) total number of schools enrolling Children with Special Needs (CwSN), number of schools with at least one dedicated special educator and number of sanctioned, filled and vacant posts of special educators, State-wise/UT-wise; and
(c) whether Government proposes to strengthen the availability of special educators by supporting States in recruitment and expanding Rehabilitation Council of India (RCI)-recognised teacher training capacity and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current status of Bharat Taxi, operated by Sahakar Taxi Cooperative Limited, including the number of registered drivers and customers, as on date;
(b) the cities in which the service is currently operational and the details of its proposed expansion to other cities, including the timeline for reaching 500 cities;
(c) the manner in which the driver-owned cooperative model is expected to ensure better earnings and welfare for drivers as compared to existing app-based ride-hailing platforms; and
(d) whether any regulatory or financial support has been extended by Government for the expansion of this initiative?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the findings of its Health Dynamics of India report indicating that only 4,413 of 13,232 sanctioned specialist posts at rural Community Health Centres are filled and Government's assessment of the present status;
(b) whether any district-wise or State-wise assessment has been undertaken to identify the factors contributing to specialist vacancies, if so, the findings thereof; and
(c) whether Government is considering establishing a dedicated rural specialist cadre with appropriate career progression and incentives, to strengthen specialist availability in rural areas, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware of instances where vehicles are detained under Section 129 of the CGST Act for minor or clerical errors in e-way bills despite existing CBIC guidelines;
(b) the number of detention orders passed under Section 129 during the last three years, State/UT-wise, along with the number of such orders subsequently set aside by appellate authorities or courts; and
(c) whether Government proposes to strengthen accountability and issue further directions to prevent wrongful detention of vehicles for technical or procedural lapses, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken note that unclaimed deposits transferred to the RBI's Depositor Education and Awareness (DEA) Fund increased from around ?67,270 crore in June 2025 to ?72,454 crore by January 2026; 
(b) whether an assessment has been made of the factors contributing to this trend, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government is examining additional measures, including proactive and time-bound outreach by banks to holders of inoperative accounts and greater integration of the UDGAM portal with Aadhaar-linked death and succession records, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware of the shortage of dedicated human resources and trained teachers in Atal Tinkering Labs (ATLs), as highlighted in recent assessments, and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the State/UT-wise number of ATLs that currently have a dedicated ATL In-Charge, an honorarium for ATL In-Charges/Assistants, and at least two trained teachers engaged in ATL activities;
(c) whether Government proposes to strengthen teacher capacity in ATLs through dedicated staffing, mandatory honorarium, and institutionalised teacher training; and
(d) if so, the details and timeline thereof, and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has taken note of emerging research indicating that excessive reliance on generative AI tools may adversely affect critical thinking and problem-solving abilities, particularly among children and young users;
(b) whether Government has any regulatory or advisory framework to address the cognitive and developmental impact of AI tool usage among children; and
(c) whether Government proposes to undertake or support India-specific research and develop age-appropriate safeguards or design standards for AI tools used by children, particularly in view of the increasing use of AI in education?

(a) the specific steps taken by the Ministry to improve 'Ease of Doing Business', including reforms in labour, land taxation, insolvency and the impact on India’s ranking in global indices;
(b) the current status of export growth and the measures adopted to achieve the target of $2 trillion exports;
(c) the details of new markets and products identified for export promotion; and
(d) the details of support provided to Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) and exporters for overcoming challenges in international trade?

(a) the current status of planned automation of litigation-related processes, including processing of Advocate Bills;
(b) the specific Departments where AI and data visualisation tools have been deployed for proactive litigation management;
(c) the number of repetitive or avoidable cases identified and withdrawn through this mechanism; and
(d) the reduction achieved in Government litigation costs as a result thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment or compliance audit of the implementation of mandatory crèche provision under the Maternity Benefit Act, 1961 (as amended in 2017) and, if so, the details and key findings thereof;
(b) whether Government maintains data on establishments required to provide crèche facilities and the extent of compliance with the said provision; and
(c) whether Government proposes to undertake a nationwide compliance assessment and issue uniform guidelines to strengthen the implementation of mandatory crèche provision?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment of ecological outcomes and environmental benefits achieved under the Green Credit Programme since its implementation, and if so, the findings thereof;
(b) whether Government has developed a framework for monitoring, verification and long-term ecological assessment of activities undertaken under the Programme;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether Government proposes to expand the scope of the Programme beyond tree plantation and water conservation to cover other environmental sectors; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether it is a fact that there exists a significant gap between the number of children legally free for adoption and registered prospective adoptive parents awaiting adoption and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the status of implementation of the Supreme Court's directions regarding District Specialised Adoption Agencies and identification of orphaned, abandoned and surrendered children eligible for adoption; and
(c) whether Government proposes to prescribe time-bound timelines for declaring eligible children legally free for adoption and strengthen the functioning of Child Care Institutions and Child Welfare Committees to reduce delays in the adoption process?

(a) the specific interventions implemented under the National Livestock Mission (NLM) to incentivise entrepreneurship in the poultry, small ruminant, porcine and animal feed sectors;
(b) the strategic framework adopted to mitigate the deficit in green fodder availability through the advancement of fodder seed production and pasture land restoration;
(c) whether specialised models for genetic breed-improvement and rural backyard entrepreneurship are being facilitated for landless and marginal livestock farmers;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the manner in which the livestock sector is being developed as a source of supplementary income and rural employment?

(a) the current status of implementation regarding the five University Townships envisioned in the Union Budget 2026-27 near prominent industrial and logistics hubs;
(b) the framework through which these hubs seek to integrate academic institutions, research facilities and centres for skill development to enhance industry-academia synergy;
(c) the current status of the constitution of the High-Powered Standing Committee on Education to Employment and Enterprise and its core mandates;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the strategic initiatives undertaken to synchronise higher education to align with labour-market needs and improve the industry-readiness of graduates?

(a) the progress achieved under the "Sahakar se Samriddhi" vision in setting up new multipurpose Primary Agriculture Cooperative Credit Societies (PACS), dairy and fishery cooperative societies in previously unserved Gram Panchayats;
(b) whether the adoption of Model Bye-Laws has successfully empowered primary societies to expand their operational scope into diverse service-delivery domains;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the specific strategies formulated to bridge regional disparities and revitalise the cooperative movement in States where its presence is relatively low?

(a) whether it is a fact that, despite blood collection in 2024-25 exceeding the national requirement of 14.6 million units, regional shortages and significant blood wastage persist and if so, Government's assessment thereof;
(b) the data on blood and blood components collected, utilised and discarded during last three years, along with category-wise reasons for such wastage, State/UT-wise and year-wise;
(c) whether Government has examined successful State blood bank management models involving centralised testing and real-time cold-chain monitoring to reduce wastage and improve transfusion safety; and
(d) if so, whether it proposes to formulate a model scheme for nationwide adoption of such best practices?

(a) whether it is a fact that the total quantity of Wheat and Rice held in the Central Pool as on 1st April, 2026 exceeded the prescribed buffer norms;
(b) whether the quantum of wheat procurement achieved during the Rabi Marketing Season 2026–27 is higher as compared to the previous season;
(c) whether Government has data on the number of farmers who benefited through Minimum Support Price (MSP) operations during the Rabi Marketing Season 2026–27;
(d) whether Government has taken steps to ensure efficient utilisation of surplus foodgrain stocks so as to optimise storage costs; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has implemented the Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) system in the fertilizer sector across the country;
(b) if so, the details of its implementation and coverage, including the number of Point of Sale (PoS) devices deployed at fertilizer retail outlets;
(c) the manner in which the DBT system has helped in curbing diversion of subsidised fertilizers and ensuring their availability to genuine farmers; 
(d) whether Government proposes to further strengthen the digital fertilizer distribution ecosystem through technological interventions and real-time monitoring mechanisms; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance that, as of December 2025, pending applications on the MSME delayed payment monitoring system involved dues of over ?31,000 crore and, if so, the assessment thereof;
(b) whether a large number of delayed payment cases remain pending at the application stage and, if so, the reasons therefor; and
(c) whether Government proposes to develop a unified AI-enabled case management system for delayed payment disputes, on the lines of e-Jagriti platform of the Department of Consumer Affairs, with features such as automated case summarisation and real-time tracking and, if so, the details and timeline thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance of the increase in complaints filed on the AirSewa portal against domestic airlines from 14,116 in 2023 to 29,042 in 2025 and if so, the reasons therefor;
(b) whether Government has taken note of concerns, including those raised by a Parliamentary Committee, regarding the gap between complaints marked as resolved and passengers actually receiving refunds or compensation; and
(c) whether Government proposes to integrate AI-based technology into the AirSewa grievance redressal system to link complaint closure with actual refund or compensation to passengers and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware that despite India being the world's second largest producer of fruits and vegetables, value addition and processing in this segment remains as low as 2 to 4.5 per cent;
(b) the reasons for this low level of processing and whether it is attributed to absence of an aggregation layer between fragmented farm-holdings and processors, resulting in high post-harvest losses before produce can reach processing units; and
(c) whether Government is considering to promote farmer-aggregation mechanisms such as FPOs or cooperatives, specifically for fruits and vegetables, on the lines of dairy cooperative model, to bridge this gap between farm and processor?

(a) the current status of crude steel production vis-à-vis the target set under the National Steel Policy, 2017;
(b) the measures taken to boost steel exports amid global trade and tariff disruptions;
(c) the steps taken to promote use of domestically produced steel in Government infrastructure projects; and
(d) the details of the strategy adopted to reduce coking coal import dependence in steel manufacturing?

(a) the number of countries with which India has signed Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) or cooperation agreements for Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI), along with the key areas of cooperation;
(b) the key details of all such agreements;
(c) the progress made in implementation of these agreements, including deployment of India's digital public goods and capacity-building initiatives in partner countries;
(d) the institutional framework adopted for coordinating DPI partnerships with partner countries and the concerned Ministries and agencies; and
(e) the roadmap for expanding India's international cooperation on Digital Public Infrastructure, particularly with countries of the Global South for the next three years?

(a) the details of progress made in the implementation of the India-European Free Trade Association (EFTA) Trade and Economic Partnership Agreement (TEPA), including the investment commitments received under the agreement;
(b) the mechanism established to monitor the commitment of a 100 billion USD investment over a period of 15 years; and
(c) the details of steps taken to promote India's exports to EFTA countries?

