(a) whether Ministry is aware that the country has only about 300–350 trained geriatricians for an elderly-population exceeding 150 million, despite the projected doubling of elderly population by 2050 and if so, details thereof;
(b) whether the Integrated Programme for Senior Citizens and other schemes under the Ministry account for this specialist shortage while planning elder-care infrastructure and number of geriatric care centres and day-care facilities currently functional under these schemes; and
