(a) whether Government is aware that India's nurse-population ratio is about 1.96 per 1,000 population as against the WHO-recommended 3 per 1,000;
(b) the number of nurses trained, registered and granted emigration clearance for overseas employment during the last three years, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of rising nurse emigration on the public health system, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government proposes to revise or increase the minimum wages/remuneration of nurses in public and private healthcare establishments, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the aggregate spending in the last five years by the PSUs and private sector entities on Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR);
